e03a8c29a4df93b32e3dfd","name":"[dev] S04 Each badge class shows on the card: New Admission, Consult, Follow-up, both contexts","fullName":"TC-01 Patient Chart Card › TC-01/S04"},"descriptionHtml":"<div class=\"rc-approach\"><p><b>Approach</b> · TC-01 Patient Chart Card · <b>S04</b> Each badge class shows on the card: New Admission, Consult, Follow-up, both contexts</p><p><b>UAT steps / ticket ACs covered:</b></p><ul><li><b>U4</b> The card shows the New Admission / Follow-up / Consult badge. (UAT TC-01; TFA-92579 AC 3)</li></ul><p><b>Test design technique: </b>Equivalence classes (equivalence) — Check the same rule again with another class of input (Hospital / Nursing Home, other data); every class has to be right.</p><p><b>Given </b>Standard fixture</p><p><b>When </b>In the chart header set Admission status to New Admission, go back to the list; repeat for Consult and Follow-up; then the same for the resident in Nursing Home</p><p><b>Then </b>After each change the list card shows exactly the chosen badge and not the other two</p><p><b>Pass rule (oracle, excerpt): </b>oracle.mjs on the list page (no other badge words there): mustContain 'Open chart for &lt;name&gt;' and the chosen badge, mustNotContain the other two. One patient per context, so not evidence for U8; the badge roll is S07</p><p><b>Where it ran: </b>dev unit U21; test method AGENT · Browser agent; lane planned in the matrix: browser agent (automated)</p><p><small>S04 is our own case number (its number in the coverage matrix cases/TC-01.matrix.json), not a step number of the UAT document.</small></p></div><p><b>Environment: dev</b> — dev deployment, build <code>43c38a4</code> (Deploy Convex, 2026-10-14T21:30:04Z); account and address are not written into the report; run folder <code>runs/2026-10-14-dev</code>.</p><p><b>Test method:</b> AGENT · Browser agent; secondary: PW · Playwright script — as classified in cases/test-methods.json, which says it runs on both; Source: <code>dev</code>.</p><p><b>UAT item:</b> TC-01 Patient Chart Card · <b>Section:</b> A1 · Home Screen &amp; Dashboard · <b>Scenario:</b> TC-01/S04</p><p><b>Each badge class shows on the card: New Admission, Consult, Follow-up, both contexts</b></p><p><b>Tickets:</b> TFA-92579 Home Screen: Patient Chart Card (ready for qa)</p><p><b>Result:</b> Pass from <code>scripts/oracle.mjs</code> on the saved evidence (<code>units/U21.verdict.json</code>), unit U21 split by its parts' checkpoints. Agent: 84 turns, 242 s, $0.68.</p><p><b>Plan:</b> unit U21 (#21, ready-for-qa, ui-only) — Admission badge set by hand. Same legacy seed, same control. TC-06 S11 runs first: its s11-n-list-before checkpoint needs the resident on Follow-up with no Consult / New Admission, which only the fresh legacy seed guarantees. TC-01 S04 then sets every badge itself and saves a checkpoint after each change, so it does not depend on where S11 left the patients. Runs together with TC-06/S11.</p><p><b>Checked by Quinn's runner</b> (<code>ledger.md</code> #21, U21; checked: yes): <b>Pass</b> — badge per chart/context never leaks (S11); all three badge states shown on list cards in both modes (S04)</p>","environment":"default","setup":[],"teardown":[],"history":[],"retries":[],"breadcrumbs":[["TC-01 Patient Chart Card","S04 Each badge class shows on the card: New Admission, Consult, Follow-up, both contexts"]],"retry":false,"titlePath":[],"retriesCount":0,"attachments":[{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"ac27dd4be8b70797f2faf48847ce382b","originalFileName":"72d76767-8d4f-49fb-bb24-a80d1365cb3f-attachment.txt","ext":".txt","contentType":"text/plain","contentLength":2538,"name":"page snapshot (accessibility tree)"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"0e54e13b58b6cdd8bfd31b5868b4e41a","originalFileName":"4c8ac806-db5c-4a23-8a97-c42aaab876cc-attachment.png","ext":".png","contentType":"image/png","contentLength":79188,"name":"screenshot"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"719bf4f2